  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    counts = Counter()\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                counts[grid[r][c]] += 1\n    \n    # Find the color that forms a compact cluster - try each non-zero color\n    # The pattern color is the one with smallest bounding box area relative to count\n    best_color = None\n    best_ratio = float('inf')\n    \n    for color, cnt in counts.items():\n        positions = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == color]\n        min_r = min(p[0] for p in positions)\n        max_r = max(p[0] for p in positions)\n        min_c = min(p[1] for p in positions)\n        max_c = max(p[1] for p in positions)\n        area = (max_r - min_r + 1) * (max_c - min_c + 1)\n        ratio = area\n        if ratio < best_ratio:\n            best_ratio = ratio\n            best_color = color\n    \n    positions = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == best_color]\n    min_r = min(p[0] for p in positions)\n    max_r = max(p[0] for p in positions)\n    min_c = min(p[1] for p in positions)\n    max_c = max(p[1] for p in positions)\n    \n    result = []\n    for r in range(min_r, max_r+1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(min_c, max_c+1):\n            row.append(best_color if grid[r][c] == best_color else 0)\n        result.append(row)\n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    counts = Counter()\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                counts[grid[r][c]] += 1\n    \n    # Find the color that forms a compact cluster - try each non-zero color\n    # The pattern color is the one with smallest bounding box area relative to count\n    best_color = None\n    best_ratio = float('inf')\n    \n    for color, cnt in counts.items():\n        positions = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == color]\n        min_r = min(p[0] for p in positions)\n        max_r = max(p[0] for p in positions)\n        min_c = min(p[1] for p in positions)\n        max_c = max(p[1] for p in positions)\n        area = (max_r - min_r + 1) * (max_c - min_c + 1)\n        ratio = area\n        if ratio < best_ratio:\n            best_ratio = ratio\n            best_color = color\n    \n    positions = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == best_color]\n    min_r = min(p[0] for p in positions)\n    max_r = max(p[0] for p in positions)\n    min_c = min(p[1] for p in positions)\n    max_c = max(p[1] for p in positions)\n    \n    result = []\n    for r in range(min_r, max_r+1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(min_c, max_c+1):\n            row.append(best_color if grid[r][c] == best_color else 0)\n        result.append(row)\n    return result",
